WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.105 --> 00:00:02.123
- All right, everybody,
let's check out social media

00:00:02.123 --> 00:00:03.930
for one last great story before we go.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.186
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:08.190
(rock music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:11.070
For parents of toddlers,
good luck first of all,

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.800
but you're lucky if your
kid finishes his peas.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.080
Not the case for a family
in Buffalo, though.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.090
This is 2-year-old, Levi,

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.380
who regularly dines on everything
from watermelon gazpacho

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.120
to squid pasta,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.630
which for a billion dollars I
couldn't get my kids to eat.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.670
His chef dad curates the menu

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.310
and posts the results on Instagram.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.660
Let's get these foodies in here.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.470
Say hi to Levi and his dad,
Jack, who watch on WKBW

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.461
in Buffalo, New York.

00:00:38.461 --> 00:00:39.294
Hi y'all.

00:00:40.503 --> 00:00:41.663
- Hi guys.

00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:45.431
- Oh my gosh, Levi, you're so cute.

00:00:45.431 --> 00:00:46.920
So, you're kind of, Jack,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.870
you're kind of his private chef, right?

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.070
- Yes, I am, yeah.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.010
Cooking has been my passion
for the last 10 years.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.200
I've worked in fine dining, catering,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.693
and cook for professional athletes,

00:00:56.693 --> 00:00:58.530
and once Levi was born,

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.320
I knew I wanted to share
my love of food with him.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.700
So, it started as early

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.980
as making all his baby food from scratch,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.370
and now it's progressed
to cooking him scallops,

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:10.620
chicken adobo, braised oxtail,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.160
and many other dishes that
even some adults haven't tried.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.800
His amazing reactions and his curiosity

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.260
when trying all these foods

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.290
led me to document our
culinary journey together.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.660
And that's how Cooking for Levi started.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.400
We wanna inspire families

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.640
to cultivate a healthy
relationship with food,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.700
and it's been a surreal
experience with the amount of love

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.130
and feedback we've gotten from everyone.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.080
And it's allowed me to
be a stay-at-home dad

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.606
and Levi's private chef.

00:01:38.606 --> 00:01:39.626
(audience laughing)

00:01:39.626 --> 00:01:41.730
- You're getting upstaged, yeah.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.110
He's like.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.376
So wait, Levi, so you have something

00:01:45.376 --> 00:01:48.390
you're about to try, right now, food wise?

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.360
- Yeah, so he actually
helped prepare this with me.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.193
- Okay.

00:01:52.193 --> 00:01:54.270
- He helped me cut up all these fruits.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:57.960
This is a, we call it the ocean parfait.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:58.793
- Wait, can you lift it?

00:01:58.793 --> 00:01:59.626
Oh, there you go.

00:01:59.626 --> 00:02:01.052
Oh, that's delicious looking.

00:02:01.052 --> 00:02:03.433
- So yeah, it's like a
little fun little idea

00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:04.478
to make with your kids.

00:02:04.478 --> 00:02:05.580
- Well, if I made it look like that

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.750
my kids would eat it.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.680
I was like, yeah.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.530
- So this is a Greek
yogurt that's colored,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.290
naturally colored with blue spirulina,

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:18.120
and then we grounded up some
graham crackers for the sand

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.720
and these are just a
bunch of different fruits.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.310
Why don't you give it a try, Levi?

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.660
- Oh my, forget Levi.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.520
I live at, I'm just kidding.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.110
I'm like, what?

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.910
That looks delicious.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:30.743
- Yeah, it's fun to be creative.

00:02:30.743 --> 00:02:32.130
- Maybe if I plated it like a beach

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.199
at Disney World, they'd eat it.

00:02:34.199 --> 00:02:36.960
Oh my God, I love it.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.750
Thank you so much for
inspiring us families.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.731
This is incredible.

00:02:41.731 --> 00:02:44.940
Aw, he's even sharing.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.830
Well, thank you so much Jack.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.290
Bye, Levi, thank you for joining us.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.011
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:51.011 --> 00:02:52.056
(bell dings)

00:02:52.056 --> 00:02:52.889
And that's not all.

00:02:52.889 --> 00:02:54.450
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.000
makers of G2 and the new G2 Edge,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.530
the go-to pens of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.770
want to honor inspiring
families just like yours,

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.090
so they're gonna be writing y'all a check

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.613
for $1,000 for a really great menu.

00:03:06.559 --> 00:03:08.310
- Thank you.
(audience cheering)

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.143
- Absolutely.

00:03:09.143 --> 00:03:09.976
Y'all have a good one

00:03:09.976 --> 00:03:11.460
and thank you all our guests this hour.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.477
Rob Gronkowski, Kali Reis,
Sydney McLaughlin-Levrone,

00:03:15.477 --> 00:03:17.910
Nicole, Madison, Logan, and Winifred.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.023
Y'all have a great day,
and if it's not, change it.

